{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code."}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Cancel Effects"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every effect the store runs is already cancelled on teardown: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and the store’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"text":" cancel all in-flight effect tasks. That is enough for cleanup, but it is ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"all-or-nothing"}]},{"text":" — you cannot cancel one specific effect while others keep running.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keyed cancellation adds that. You give an effect a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"cancel id"}]},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and later cancel every effect running under that id with the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" effect or the imperative ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" method. Identity lives outside the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" type — it is still a plain closure — so nothing about reducer signatures changes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reach for this when an effect outlives the action that started it: cancelling text-to-speech when the user skips, debouncing a search field, or tearing down a long-lived listener when a screen disappears.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Choosing an id","anchor":"Choosing-an-id","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A cancel id is any ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable & Sendable"},{"text":" value. Distinct ids are independent; effects sharing an id are cancelled together. A dedicated empty type reads well and can’t collide with another feature’s id:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["private enum SearchID: Hashable, Sendable {}","private enum SpeechID: Hashable, Sendable {}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Strings and enums work too — pick whatever is unambiguous in your domain.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Cancel from inside a reducer","anchor":"Cancel-from-inside-a-reducer","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Return ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to tag the work, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to stop it:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["case .startSpeaking(let text):","    return cancellable(id: SpeechID()) { send in","        for await word in speech.speak(text) {","            await send(.spokeWord(word))","        }","    }","","case .skip:","    \/\/ Stop any in-flight speech immediately.","    return cancel(id: SpeechID())"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the speaking effect is cancelled, its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"text":" loop ends at the next suspension point, exactly as it would on teardown.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Debounce with `cancelInFlight`","anchor":"Debounce-with-cancelInFlight","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Passing ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancelInFlight: true"},{"text":" cancels any effect already running under the id ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"text":" starting the new one — the whole of debounce in one line:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["case .queryChanged(let query):","    return cancellable(id: SearchID(), cancelInFlight: true) { send in","        try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(300))","        let results = try await api.search(query)","        await send(.results(results))","    }"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each keystroke re-dispatches ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".queryChanged"},{"text":"; the new effect cancels the previous sleeping one, so only the last query in a burst reaches the network.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Cancel from view or scene code","anchor":"Cancel-from-view-or-scene-code","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When there is no reducer action to hang the cancellation on — a screen disappearing, a sheet dismissing — call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" directly:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".onDisappear {","    store.cancel(id: SearchID())","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ids with nothing running are ignored, so it is always safe to call.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What it does not replace","anchor":"What-it-does-not-replace","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keyed cancellation is not a substitute for resource cleanup. An effect holding a file handle, a network connection, or an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"text":" continuation should still release it — use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTaskCancellationHandler"},{"text":" or a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"defer"},{"text":". Cancellation ends the task; it does not close what the task opened.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Effects that terminate on their own (a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"text":" loop whose stream finishes) need no id at all. Only reach for a cancel id when something ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"else"}]},{"text":" has to stop the effect early.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"How-to-Guides","title":"How-to Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects"]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/cancel(id:)":{"title":"cancel(id:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/cancel(id:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An effect that cancels every in-flight effect running under "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)":{"title":"cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancellable","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancelInFlight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelinflight:_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tags an effect with a cancellation identity so it can later be cancelled by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"Store.cancel(id:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"title":"Add a Parental Gate","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge."}],"role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddPersistence":{"title":"Add Persistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" macro — no hand-written "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" classes, database actors, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}],"role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancelEffects()":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancelEffects"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancels all in-flight effects."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/canceleffects()","title":"cancelEffects()"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"title":"Add Analytics","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify."}],"role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddICloudSync":{"title":"Add iCloud Sync","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddicloudsync","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer opt-in, cross-device iCloud sync on top of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxCloudKitSync"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin — including a runtime opt-out toggle, launch-time entitlement detection, and the Apple Developer portal configuration."}],"role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"title":"Add a Version Killswitch","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkillswitch","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that prevents unsupported app versions from running, with an “Update” path back to the App Store."}],"role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancel(id:)":{"title":"cancel(id:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/cancel(id:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancels every in-flight effect tagged with "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" via"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Install the bundled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swidux-ref"},{"type":"text","text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand."}],"role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAPaywall":{"title":"Add a Paywall","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase."}],"role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"title":"Building a Domain Plugin","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddFeatureFlags":{"title":"Add Feature Flags","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config."}],"role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","title":"Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"title":"Effect","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}]}}}